UID:dothebay-17830872@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:David Lynch cemented his reputation as an uncompromising visio
 nary with BLUE VELVET\, one of the most controversial films of the 1980s\,
  burrowing beneath the surface of idyllic suburban America to reveal a sin
 ister underworld of sex and violence. After stumbling upon a severed human
  ear\, a young college student (Kyle MacLachlan) becomes obsessed with inv
 estigating its origins and gets entangled with a nightclub chanteuse (Isab
 ella Rossellini) and her psychopathic lover (Dennis Hopper). A masterfully
  eerie\, depraved psychosexual nightmare and one of the greatest films of 
 the 1980s.\n\n“Frank Booth is the role Dennis Hopper was born and chemic
 ally mutated to own. Sometimes David Lynch can teeter too far into the abs
 urdity for absurdity's sake\, but BLUE VELVET remains perfectly balanced a
 s it dives into the dark\, bizarre underbelly of society that lurks just b
 elow the surface of suburbia. It is also worth noting that BLUE VELVET\, w
 hen screened in the first month of operation at the original Alamo\, was t
 he movie that inspired our strict no-talking policy.” (Tim League\, Alam
 o Drafthouse founder)\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/bl
 ue-velvet-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7562198;-122.419185
