DESCRIPTION:- Class Time: 7:00PM - 10:00PM\n\nIn Beginner's Leatherworking
 : Craft Your Own Tri-fold Leather Journal\, you will learn and apply leath
 erworking techniques to create a custom\, refillable journal from vegetabl
 e tanned leather! We will teach you how to use a pattern to mark and punch
  holes\, set eyelets\, and attach a leather pocket using either saddle sti
 tching or rivets. You will also learn the basics of leather stamping and s
 taining as you customize the journal cover and interior pocket. Finally\, 
 you will install the elastic band\, add your journal inserts\, and finish 
 the piece with a custom button or charm. Each student will leave class wit
 h one handmade leather journal and a working knowledge of the tools and te
 chniques needed to continue exploring leatherworking at home!\n\nSupplies 
 Needed: None. All leather supplies are included to complete this project. 
 Each student will also receive two Moleskine journals in either ruled or p
 lain page styles to complete their refillable leather journal.\n\nThe rule
 s / important stuff: We have a NO EXCEPTIONS 72 HOUR CANCELLATION policy -
  this includes cancellation\, re-books\, gift certificates\, moving classe
 s\, etc. For more information on canceling a class\, please read our cance
 llation policy. All classes are 21+. If any questions\, please email us at
  info AT workshopsf DOT org.\n\nALL CLASSES TAKE PLACE AT WORKSHOP SF LOCA
 TED AT 1310 HAIGHT STREET UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED ON THE TITLE AND LISTING.
 \n\n$73.75\n\nTickets: https://etix.prf.hn/click/camref:1011l3GdWo/pubref:
