DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Manufacturing Week with a behind-the-scenes tour of 
 two innovative Dogpatch businesses.\n\nVisit Rickshaw Bagworks\, where ski
 lled craftspeople design and sew durable bags by hand\, and Wildtype\, a p
 ioneering food company using cutting-edge technology to cultivate seafood 
 from cells. Presented in partnership with the Dogpatch Art & Business Asso
 ciation\, this tour explores the breadth of modern manufacturing-from time
 -honored craftsmanship to groundbreaking food science.\n\n4:00 - Meet at W
 oods Yard Park (915 22nd Street at the corner of 22nd and Minnesota)\n\n4:
 05 - Rickshaw Bagworks (904 22nd St.)\n\n5:00 - Wildtype (2525 3rd St.)\n\
 nFree\n\nPresented by San Francisco Public Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco 
 Public Library\n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl.org/Made-in-SF-26\nDetails: htt
 ps://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/6/made-in-sf-handcrafted-to-high-tech-man
 ufacturing-in-dogpatch-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
