BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Money in San Francisco politics: Who’s spending big on the elect
 ion?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17761032@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Activism
DESCRIPTION:Wealthy special interests are trying to grab more power in San
  Francisco — whether they succeed is up to voters.\n\nAt\na time when pu
 blic oversight is shrinking and power is being\nconcentrated fewer hands\,
  understanding the role of large campaign\ndonors in our political process
  has never been more urgent.\n\nJoin\nJoe Rivano Barros of Mission Local f
 or an in-depth look at who is\nspending millions on San Francisco's Novemb
 er 2026 ballot propositions\nin an effort to influence your vote. You'll l
 earn how these megadonors\nare trying to change the outcome of the electio
 n to serve the few\, not\nthe many.\n\nAfter\nJoe's presentation\, Lila La
 Hood of the San Francisco Public Press will\nmoderate a panel discussion o
 n money in local politics with Darius Kemp\nof California Common Cause and
  Patrick Ford of the San Francisco Ethics\nCommission\, with time for ques
 tions from the audience.\n\nSpeakers\n\nJoe Rivano Barros\, Executive Edit
 or\, Mission Local – Joe is an award-winning journalist whose coverage f
 ocuses on\npolitics\, campaign finance\, Silicon Valley\, and criminal jus
 tice. He\nreceived a B.A. at Stanford University for political science in 
 2014. He\nwas born in Sweden\, grew up in Chile\, and moved to Oakland whe
 n he was\neight.\n\nPatrick Ford\, Executive Director\, San Francisco Ethi
 cs Commission – Pat has served as the Ethics Commission's Executive Dire
 ctor since\nJanuary 2024\, after joining in 2017 as Director of Enforcemen
 t. He leads\nthe agency's mission to administer campaign finance laws\, in
 vestigate...\n\nFree\nLeague of Women Voters and San Francisco Public Pres
 s\n\nTickets: https://luma.com/3tgmuo29?utm_source=dothebay\nDetails: http
 s://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/8/money-in-san-francisco-politics-who-s-sp
 ending-big-on-the-election-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34038637/c7376887-cde6-479e-8f38-d96f340a3281.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Internet Archive\, 300 Funston Avenue\, San Francisco\, CA\, 9411
 8
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/8/money-in-san-francisco-politics-
 who-s-spending-big-on-the-election-tickets
