BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Off the Grid Treasure Island
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17260589@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Food & Drink
DESCRIPTION:Off the Grid Treasure Island\nSaturdays | 11am–4pm | Citysid
 e Park\, Treasure Island\n\nRSVP FOR YOUR FREE ROUNDTRIP FERRY PASS!\n\nEv
 ery Saturday\, September 12 - October 17 from 11 AM to 4 PM\, Off the Grid
  returns to Treasure Island\, bringing food trucks\, music\, and family-fr
 iendly activities to Cityside Park in San Francisco’s newest waterfront 
 neighborhood.\n\nThe Fall series includes free kite flying\, face painting
 \, and plenty of open space to relax\, making it an easy outing for all ag
 es. Admission is free\, and complimentary ferry service from the San Franc
 isco Ferry Building is available with RSVP.\n\nEach pass is valid for one 
 guest and one free roundtrip ferry ride to and from Off the Grid Treasure 
 Island. Passes are limited and do not reserve or guarantee a specific ferr
 y departure time.\n\nWhat to Expect:\n\nOne Island. 15+ Creators. Multiple
  Cuisines.\nMore than 15 food creators per event span Vietnamese\, Korean\
 , Japanese\, Hawaiian\, Mexican\, Italian\, German\, BBQ\, fried chicken\,
  sandwiches\, and sweets. There’s something for every craving\, from go-
 to favorites to something entirely new.\n\nA Waterfront Setting with Unbea
 table Views\nCityside Park spans six acres along the shoreline\, with open
  lawns\, wide promenades\, and views that stretch from the Bay Bridge to t
 he Golden Gate. Settle in\, explore the park\, and take in the full sweep 
 of the Bay.\n\nKites Over the Bay\nThe signature kite program returns\, wi
 th complimentary kites available with signup. By midday\, the sky fills wi
 th color\, cr...\n\nFree\, All ages\nOff the Grid Presents\n\nTickets: htt
 ps://www.tisf.com/off-the-grid\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/weekl
 y/sat/off-the-grid-treasure-island-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/31665304/885c1fe6-f714-4d63-a71e-9afd592d3e9f.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Cityside Park\, Treasure Island\, 387 Avenue of the Palms\, San F
 rancisco\, CA\, 94130
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/weekly/sat/off-the-grid-treasure-island-ti
 ckets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heather Hardcastle\, The Flour Craft Bakery & Cafe Cookbook
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261010T130000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17654583@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Shopping
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, October 10\, 2026\, 11:00 am - 11:45 am\n\nStop by 
 the Foodwise Classroom for a cooking demo featuring the seasonal bounty of
  the Ferry Plaza Farmers Market.\n\nHeather Hardcastle is the chef and fou
 nder of Flour Craft Bakery & Café\, a beloved Marin County institution sh
 e opened in 2010. For more than 15 years long before gluten-free went main
 stream she has quietly reshaped the conversation around gluten-free food b
 y building Flour Craft around what people genuinely love to eat\, rather t
 han what they have to do without. Her beautiful pastries\, thoughtful seas
 onal cooking\, and California-inspired sensibility have grown the bakery\,
  with locations in Mill Valley and San Anselmo\, into one of the Bay Areas
  most cherished gluten-free destinations\, drawing a fiercely loyal commun
 ity that returns simply because they love the food.\n\nHeather is also the
  author of The Flour Craft Bakery & Cafe Cookbook: Inspired Gluten Free Re
 cipes for Breakfast\, Lunch\, Tea\, and Celebrations\, a collection of app
 roachable\, seasonal recipes that reflect her belief that everyone deserve
 s exceptional food. At this event\, Heather will lead a live cooking demon
 stration\, followed by a signing of her cookbook a chance to cook alongsid
 e her\, taste her approach to gluten-free baking\, and take home a signed 
 copy.\n\nAll demos take place in the Foodwise Classroom (green tent in fro
 nt of the Ferry Building) and are free to the public\, with recipes and sa
 mples for all.\n\nThe demo will be followed by a book signing w...\n\nTick
 ets: https://foodwise.org/events/heather-hardcastle-the-flour-craft-bakery
 -cafe-cookbook/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/heather-h
 ardcastle-the-flour-craft-bakery-cafe-cookbook-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33535004/e445e13f-93a0-4679-84f9-8dd6fcc7f705.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Ferry Plaza
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/heather-hardcastle-the-flour-cr
 aft-bakery-cafe-cookbook-tickets
END:VEVENT
