DESCRIPTION:Elephant Gym successfully completed a world tour spanning 60 c
 ities across 23 countries. However\, behind this achievement lay an unseen
  crisis of disbandment\, along with hidden conflicts and struggles. What d
 oes it truly mean to be a band?\n\nThe film was first screened in October 
 2025 at the Kaohsiung Film Festival\, one of Taiwan’s leading film festi
 vals\, and will also be shown in theaters in both Japan and Taiwan. While 
 their world tour across 23 countries and 60 cities was a major success\, t
 he film reveals the untold story behind it—including a looming breakup c
 risis during its preparation\, as well as the band’s internal conflicts 
 and struggles.\n\n“If your dreams were to become reality\, what price wo
 uld you be willing to pay?“\n\nElephant Gym\, an instrumental band from 
 Kaohsiung\, Taiwan\, has been creating indie music since its formation in 
 2012. Their sound blends complex rhythms with irregular time signatures an
 d sophisticated melodies. In Taiwan\, their avant-garde musical style ofte
 n raised the question: who would even listen to this?\n\nHowever\, in 2024
 \, they embarked on a world tour covering 23 countries and 60 shows\, incl
 uding three performances in the Philippines. They captivated audiences wor
 ldwide and firmly established their presence. Yet behind the glamorous sta
 ge\, there were deep struggles.\n\nBetween guitarist Tell Chang and bassis
 t KT Chang—who are siblings—there were conflicts between family ties a
 nd band dynamics. Drummer Chia-Chin Tu had to make the difficult decisi...
 \n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/19867?siteToken=d
 2atbcege5knqsavntt91g1250\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11
 /elephant-gym-more-real-than-dreams-tickets-qed9wx8\nSource: DoTheBay
