BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:San Francisco Indigenous Peoples Day w/ special performance by Jer
 emy Dutcher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T140000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17207818@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Free RSVP\n\nJoin us in celebration of San Francisco Indigenou
 s Peoples Day with a magnificent profusion of Native American art\, music 
 and vendors. The event highlights the vastly diverse and talented communit
 y of Indigenous artists in the Bay Area\, California and the Americas. Pre
 sented on Yelamu\, Ramaytush Ohlone Territory\, in partnership with the In
 ternational Indian Treaty Council\, the program at Yerba Buena Gardens fol
 lows the Annual Indigenous Peoples Day Sunrise Gathering on Alcatraz – p
 lease check the IITC website for updates. Schedule to be announced.\n\nA g
 roundbreaking Indigenous musician whose art flows directly out of his cult
 ural activism\, tenor Jeremy Dutcher is a conservatory-trained Canadian co
 mposer\, musicologist and performer who has turned European classical musi
 c into a vehicle for language preservation. A member of Neqotkuk First Nat
 ion in Eastern Canada now based in Montréal\, Québec\, Dutcher catapulte
 d to renown with his debut album Wolastoqiyik Lintuwakonawa\, which won th
 e 2018 Polaris Music Prize and the Juno Award for Indigenous Music Album o
 f the Year at the Canadian equivalent of the Grammys in 2019. The project 
 unearthed century-old archival recordings of his ancestors\, which he turn
 ed into collaborative compositions on piano. Sung entirely in Wolastoqey\,
  his endangered mother tongue\, the album led to collaborations with artis
 ts such as Yo-Yo Ma and Feist. His follow-up release\, 2023’s Motewolonu
 wok\, was also awarded the Polaris Music Prize\, making Du...\n\nFree\nInt
 ernational Inadian Treaty Council + Yerba Buena Gardens Festival Present\n
 \nTickets: https://ybgfestival.org/event/indigenous-peoples-day-jeremy-dut
 cher/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/12/san-francisco-indig
 enous-peoples-day-with-special-performance-by-jeremy-dutcher-tickets\nSour
 ce: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7850153;-122.4023464
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/31425255/f96f8a7b-fd59-4dca-b19f-d37561c4aa6a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Yerba Buena Gardens covers two square city blocks bounded by Miss
 ion\, Folsom\, Third and Fourth Streets.\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/12/san-francisco-indigenous-people
 s-day-with-special-performance-by-jeremy-dutcher-tickets
END:VEVENT
